speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, under the provisions of Standing Order 43, I seek the unanimous consent of the House to introduce a motion dealing with an important matter of pressing necessity.
Considering that the cost of living has increased substantially over the past months, becoming a source of concern and economic restraint for old age security pensioners;
Considering that costs are rising more quickly than the quarterly increase of old age security and guaranteed income supplement;
Considering that it is the duty of the government to continue to look after the present and future needs of senior citizens tackling inflation and the ever increasing cost of living;
I move, seconded by the hon. member for Champlain (Mr. Matte):

February 17, 1978
That the House enjoin the Minister of National Health and Welfare to take all necessary steps to introduce a bill to increase old age security benefits to $225 a month and to raise the guaranteed income supplement accordingly.
